{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386890-so-i-made-npcs","id":1386890,"title":"So I made NPCs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-08T20:23:04-07:00","id":1386890,"title":"So I made NPCs","content":"So I'm working on a Philippine M20 setting and I came up with for some Mage Manila characters.<br /> Traditions:<a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zp28vbdiR9Gz7e8R70fPcDvScMzEWcr3/view\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zp2...ScMzEWcr3/view</a><br /> Technocracy:<a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fHmNg_fk4Oqei8Lz0ao_URDeBCgI-hJy/view\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fHm...eBCgI-hJy/view</a><br /> <br /> Comments and suggestions are very welcome.<br /> <br /> I also have a link for these on my blog - <a href=\"https://godegeekery.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://godegeekery.wordpress.com/</a> - but a lot of these blog posts are unrelated to the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there are typos and inconsistencies here and there. I wrote the rotes/adjustments the way I did as a quick guide for my use if I were to run a game with these characters and the format was meant for whan i run games on my laptop.<br /> <br /> So I'm planning to make a few Adventures for mage set in the Philippines, the first of which is a Tradition game of establishing a Council Chantry in Intramuros, which will probably involve doing something about the numerous spirits that have been haunting the place since WWII and interactions with some other things that would spoil the surprise if I explained exactly what they were. For the Traditions, most are not from the Philippines but are there because they have a good reason to be there. I plan to create more local Philippine mage NPCs in the Adentures themselves, as opposed to the Technocracy which will probably have more NPCs showing up from outside the country in their own adventures. I have to finish a bit of my own stuff before getting to these though, but woud love to hear about the sorts of adventures players might go for in a Philippine Mage game. I have no idea what I'll be doing for the Technocracy side of things quite yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T22:16:27-07:00","id":1386910,"title":"","content":"Traditions characters look pretty good. I like Sam the Chakravanti as a different take on that character. For your Philippine M20 setting, the Tradition characters look pretty powerful--high Arete and pretty high spheres. Are they intended to be mentors to new PCs or are you looking to make it so someone could just use them and jump in with some powerful mages?<br /> <br /> Next Technocracy Reloaded section drops on Tuesday, so that might be a better time to review those characters as based on chapter order we should get the Technocracy factions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T22:27:57-07:00","id":1386913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386890-so-i-made-npcs?p=1386910#post1386910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For your Philippine M20 setting, the Tradition characters look pretty powerful--high Arete and pretty high spheres. Are they intended to be mentors to new PCs or are you looking to make it so someone could just use them and jump in with some powerful mages?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both actually. It wouldn't make sense for the Traditions to send a bunch of noobs to establish an important multi tradition chantry meant to hold their designated survivors,and that's my first adventure plan for them. So, for a starting character game they'd make up the local leadership and mentors but for more advanced games they'd be PCs or Allies/Enemies<br /> <br /> Edit: I can even see a Technocracy game where they are your Villains roster","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T22:34:02-07:00","id":1387187,"title":"","content":"Sorry to bother whoever I might bother with this, but here goes:<br /> <br /> When someone suggested my sticking the NPCs and other White-Wolf based stuff I plan to make in the Storyteller's Vault, I thought it was just like some subforum or something where people put their WOD based works so that Storytellers could easily access them. I think someone told me a long time ago I had to put stuff in a specific format for the Vault and so I thought that figuring that out would be my only problem. After a bit of searching, I find the Storyteller's Vault site and will have to say I am a just bit confused by what I am looking at.<br /> <br /> It looks like a WOD product site where I can publish my own works and I have to just read through and follow the rules to do so???<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T09:06:04-07:00","id":1387284,"title":"","content":"The Storytellers Vault is a WoD product site for fan-based works in the WoD. You can even use their art resources for layout. You can charge for your work and since it's part of the One Bookshelf family that includes drivethrurpg.com, it's a big platform for WoD work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://storytellersvault.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/categories/115000125912-Storytellers-Vault-General-Information\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://storytellersvault.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/categories/115000125912-Storytellers-Vault-General-Information\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://storytellersvault.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/categories/115000125912-Storytellers-Vault-General-Information\" target=\"_blank\"> https://storytellersvault.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/categories/115000125912-Storytellers-Vault-General-Information </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://storytellersvault.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/115000956871-Why-should-I-participate-in-the-Storytellers-Vault-\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://storytellersvault.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/115000956871-Why-should-I-participate-in-the-Storytellers-Vault-\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://storytellersvault.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/115000956871-Why-should-I-participate-in-the-Storytellers-Vault-\" target=\"_blank\"> https://storytellersvault.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/115000956871-Why-should-I-participate-in-the-Storytellers-Vault- </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T11:21:26-07:00","id":1387300,"title":"","content":"Awesome. I guess I'll give it a try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2